Instructions in the PTX: `mma.sync.aligned.m16n8k16.row.col.f32.bf16.bf16.f32`, `mma.sync.aligned.m16n8k16.row.col.f32.f16.f16.f32`


## Part E: the order of the chunks

For chunks x < y and k (all distinct, chunks of 16 consecutive k): +B at a random position of chunk x, -B in chunk y, a small product s in chunk k, with B/s = 2^28, beyond the window. s survives exactly when chunk k is accumulated after both x and y (before, it is cut against B; between, too). `agree`: triples whose outcome is that of increasing k.

| operands | M x N, warps | path | chunks | triples | agree with increasing k |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| float16 | 64 x 64, 4 | mma.sync | 8 | 168 | 168 |
| rejected: out of resources on this device |  |
| float16 | 16 x 16, 1 | mma.sync | 8 | 168 | 168 |
| float16 | 16 x 16, 1 | mma.sync | 32 | 3000 | 3000 |
| bfloat16 | 64 x 64, 4 | mma.sync | 8 | 168 | 168 |
| rejected: out of resources on this device |  |
| bfloat16 | 16 x 16, 1 | mma.sync | 8 | 168 | 168 |
| bfloat16 | 16 x 16, 1 | mma.sync | 32 | 3000 | 3000 |

