| bfloat16 | 16 x 16, 1 | 256 | bf16x3 | subwin, sub, softmax, subrand, bits | 1280 | 1280 |
| bfloat16 | 16 x 16, 1 | 256 | bf16x6 | subwin, sub, softmax, subrand, bits | 1280 | 1280 |

### G2: the fp8 chunk facts on `mma.sync` with a subnormal `float8e5` operand

On `mma.sync` Triton converts fp8 operands to `float16` (a subnormal `float8e5` value is a subnormal `float16` value) and runs two `float16` instructions per chunk of 32. One product per chunk of 16 has a subnormal `float8e5` operand and a large partner, so its field is the smallest normal's; the other products lie just below that `float16` window's unit and are lost (only `float8e5` by `float8e5` has normal products that small). The error against `DotE5m2Chunk`'s implied interval, on `16 x 16` with 1 warp.

| operands | path | K | rows | largest error / chunk facts' bound | largest error / magnitude sum |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| e5 x e5 | mma.sync | 32 | 16 | 0.000098 | 1.04e-06 |
| e5 x e5 | mma.sync | 64 | 16 | 0.000098 | 1.56e-06 |
| e5 x e5 | mma.sync | 256 | 16 | 0.000032 | 9.27e-07 |

### G3: `tl.dot_scaled` (`"e4m3"` by `"e4m3"`) on window inputs

`DotScaledE4m3`'s domain `scaledDomBF16` admits only `0` and normal `bfloat16` scaled values, so the emulated `bfloat16` dot has no subnormal operand. Per chunk of 16 one product `448 * 448` (scale `2^0`) and 15 products of `1.875 * 2^-6` (normal `e4m3`, and a subnormal `e4m3` element `2^-9`, which `bfloat16` holds as a normal value), lost below the window; the error against the fact's bound `relDot16 K mag + absDot16 K`.

| fast_math | K | rows | largest error / bound | every scaled value in scaledDomBF16 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| False | 32 | 16 | 0.005451 | True |
| False | 64 | 16 | 0.002808 | True |
| False | 256 | 16 | 0.000722 | True |
| True | 32 | 16 | 0.005451 | True |
| True | 64 | 16 | 0.002808 | True |
| True | 256 | 16 | 0.000739 | True |

